  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` and it passes `typecheck`. I could not run `vite build` or open it in a browser. Nothing has been rendered, so the visuals and the engine calls below are untested.\n\nThe scene is a standing stone ring made of 36 weathered blocks, with glowing cyan and violet rune strips on its inner face. It sits on a round stone platform that has a violet inlay. Six pillars (two of them broken), rubble and fallen column drums surround it. The sky is a dusk gradient with a warm low sun, fog, bloom, a colour grade and a vignette.\n\n- **Energy disc:** a custom GLSL shader draws the vortex. It has cyan and violet spiral arms that twist tighter toward the centre, a bright white core and a bright rim. Two additive halo discs add glow around the ring. A `clock` uniform animates all three every frame.\n- **Coloured light:** cyan, violet and blue-violet point lights light the stones and platform. Their intensity pulses slowly through `setLight`, and I did not confirm that call takes effect.\n- **Particles:** three instanced-sphere pools, with about 240 particles live at steady state. There are cyan and violet spirals that move into the portal, and pale motes that rise from the platform and shrink away. Each pool has a CPU-side spawn rate, lifetime and live slot count, and the pools are pre-simulated so the first frame is already populated.\n- **Camera:** a slow sway of about ±0.4 rad around the portal with a small height bob and distance change. It is driven by `app.camera.setPose` each frame, which I did not confirm works in this build.\n- **Contract:** `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { portalActive: true, particleCount, time }` is updated every frame, where `particleCount` is the live total across the pools. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first engine frame callback, and the engine owns the animation-frame loop.\n\n",
